response.rawText:
{"text":"Mild redness after using a TENS unit can be normal and is often caused by increased circulation, pressure from the electrode, or mild skin sensitivity. It should typically fade shortly after removing the pads. To reduce skin irritation: Make sure your skin is clean and dry before use. Avoid placing pads on irritated or damaged skin. Rotate pad placement between treatments. Reduce treatment intensity if the sensation feels uncomfortable. Replace electrodes when the gel becomes old or irritating.

Useful Resources & Links:
📋 [TENS Electrode Placement Chart](https://paintechnology.s3.amazonaws.com/pdf/placementchart.pdf)"}

